# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback (CF-1).
#
# Every non-asset path serves index.html with a 200, so a deep link or a hard
# refresh on an in-app route resolves instead of 404ing. Cloudflare Pages tries
# a real file first, so hashed assets, /constants/pack.json, /sw.js and friends
# are unaffected — this only catches what would otherwise be a miss.
#
# 200, not 302: a redirect would rewrite the address bar and lose the route the
# user actually asked for. The client router reads location and takes it from
# there.
#
# The GitHub Pages path solves this differently — deploy-public.yml copies
# index.html to 404.html, because Pages has no rewrite rules at all. That trick
# stays confined to that workflow; this file is the Cloudflare answer.
/*    /index.html    200
